reated_at":"2025-07-27T01:08:03Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T18:53:45Z","closed_at":"2026-07-22T18:53:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5beta, 4.5beta.double\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta.double (2d113cc22) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu, 24 Jul 2025 18:18:11 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (nvidia; 575.64.05) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 154.8 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf a shader file contains a struct comparison, then when the editor processes that file, it crashes.\n\n```gdshader\nshader_type spatial;\nstruct foo { int x; };\nvoid func () {\n  foo a;\n  a == a;\n}\n```\n\nThis crashes the editor. If `a == a` is commented out, it does not crash the editor.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Make a project, add a shader file containing the above code.\n1. The editor crashes.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug-shader-crash_2025-07-27_02-03-22.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21450720/bug-shader-crash_2025-07-27_02-03-22.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Re